---
description: TypeScript + React patterns for DCIM
globs: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: false
---

## TypeScript
- Prefer `unknown` over `any`.
- Keep types in `DCIM Compliance App/src/types.ts` (or colocate for small local types).
- Avoid broad unions that erase meaning; model domain concepts (facility, compliance status, evidence package).

## React 18 patterns
- Use `useMemo` / `useDeferredValue` for expensive filtering.
- Use `useCallback` for handlers passed into memoized children.
- Prefer conditional rendering (`{show && <X/>}`), not `display: none`.
- Always add `useEffect` cleanup.

## UI constraints (important)
- No dynamic Tailwind class generation.
- Prefer inline styles for dynamic colors.
- Avoid huge components; split if files approach ~50KB.

